      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the base seven sum of the digits of the product of the base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base seven numbers to base ten.\n2. Multiply the base ten numbers.\n3. Convert the product back to base seven.\n4. Find the base seven sum of the digits of the product.\n\n**Step 1: Convert the base seven numbers to base ten.**\n\nThe base seven number \\(24_7\\) can be converted to base ten as follows:\n\\[24_7 = 2 \\times 7^1 + 4 \\times 7^0 = 2 \\times 7 + 4 \\times 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}.\\]\n\nThe base seven number \\(30_7\\) can be converted to base ten as follows:\n\\[30_7 = 3 \\times 7^1 + 0 \\times 7^0 = 3 \\times 7 + 0 \\times 1 = 21_{10}.\\]\n\n**Step 2: Multiply the base ten numbers.**\n\nNow, we multiply the base ten equivalents:\n\\[18_{10} \\times 21_{10} = 378_{10}.\\]\n\n**Step 3: Convert the product back to base seven.**\n\nTo convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base seven, we need to divide by 7 and keep track of the remainders:\n\\[378 \\div 7 = 54 \\text{ remainder } 0,\\]\n\\[54 \\div 7 = 7 \\text{ remainder } 5,\\]\n\\[7 \\div 7 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 0,\\]\n\\[1 \\div 7 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 1.\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(378_{10} = 1050_7\\).\n\n**Step 4: Find the base seven sum of the digits of the product.**\n\nThe base seven number \\(1050_7\\) can be converted back to base ten to find the sum of its digits:\n\\[1050_7 = 1 \\times 7^3 + 0 \\times 7^2 + 5 \\times 7^1 + 0 \\times 7^0 = 1 \\times 343 + 0 \\times 49 + 5 \\times 7 + 0 \\times 1 = 343 + 35 = 378_{10}.\\]\n\nThe sum of the digits of \\(1050_7\\) is:\n\\[1 + 0 + 5 + 0 = 6.\\]\n\nThus, the base seven sum of the digits of the product is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
