      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to convert the base seven numbers \\(24_7\\) and \\(30_7\\) to base ten, perform the multiplication in base ten, and then convert the result back to base seven. Finally, we will find the sum of the digits of the resulting base seven number.\n\nFirst, convert \\(24_7\\) to base ten:\n\\[\n24_7 = 2 \\cdot 7^1 + 4 \\cdot 7^0 = 2 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 4 = 18_{10}\n\\]\n\nNext, convert \\(30_7\\) to base ten:\n\\[\n30_7 = 3 \\cdot 7^1 + 0 \\cdot 7^0 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 0 \\cdot 1 = 21_{10}\n\\]\n\nNow, multiply the base ten equivalents:\n\\[\n18_{10} \\times 21_{10} = 378_{10}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to convert \\(378_{10}\\) to base seven. We do this by finding the largest power of 7 that fits into 378 and then breaking down the number step by step.\n\nThe powers of 7 are:\n\\[\n7^0 = 1, \\quad 7^1 = 7, \\quad 7^2 = 49, \\quad 7^3 = 343, \\quad 7^4 = 2401\n\\]\nWe see that \\(7^3 = 343\\) is the largest power of 7 that fits into 378.\n\nNow, divide 378 by 343 to find the coefficient for \\(7^3\\):\n\\[\n378 \\div 343 \\approx 1.09265 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 1 \\cdot 343 = 343\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient for \\(7^3\\) is 1. Subtract 343 from 378 to find the remainder:\n\\[\n378 - 343 = 35\n\\]\n\nNext, divide 35 by 49 to find the coefficient for \\(7^2\\):\n\\[\n35 \\div 49 \\approx 0.7142857 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 0 \\cdot 49 = 0\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient for \\(7^2\\) is 0. Subtract 0 from 35 to find the remainder:\n\\[\n35 - 0 = 35\n\\]\n\nNext, divide 35 by 49 to find the coefficient for \\(7^1\\):\n\\[\n35 \\div 49 \\approx 0.7142857 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 0 \\cdot 49 = 0\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient for \\(7^1\\) is 0. Subtract 0 from 35 to find the remainder:\n\\[\n35 - 0 = 35\n\\]\n\nFinally, divide 35 by 49 to find the coefficient for \\(7^0\\):\n\\[\n35 \\div 49 \\approx 0.7142857 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 0 \\cdot 49 = 0\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient for \\(7^0\\) is 0. Subtract 0 from 35 to find the remainder:\n\\[\n35 - 0 = 35\n\\]\n\nHowever, we notice that there was a miscalculation in the previous step. Let's correct it:\n\\[\n35 \\div 49 = \\frac{35}{49} = \\frac{35}{49} = 0.7142857 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 0 \\cdot 49 = 0\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient for \\(7^1\\) is 0. Subtract 0 from 35 to find the remainder:\n\\[\n35 - 0 = 35\n\\]\n\\[\n35 \\div 49 = \\frac{35}{49} = \\frac{35}{49} = 0.7142857 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 0 \\cdot 49 = 0\n\\]\nSo, the coefficient for \\(7^0\\) is 1. Subtract 1 from 35 to find the remainder:\n\\[\n35 - 1 = 34\n\\]\n\nThus, the base seven representation of 378 is:\n\\[\n378_{10} = 1000_7\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the sum of the digits of \\(1000_7\\):\n\\[\n1 + 0 + 0 + 0 = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the digits of the product in base seven is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).",
